# Rust
/target/
**/target/
# Cargo.lock is committed: this workspace produces binaries (cli/mcp/app),
# and pinned deps matter for reproducible builds across contributors.

# Node / frontend (Tauri UI)
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local

# Tauri
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Media test fixtures (large binaries don't belong in git)
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv
*.wav
!tests/fixtures/**/*.md

# Scratch
/scratch/
/tmp/

# Harness-only test media (docs/preview-webview.md P1 harness verification) — generated
# locally with ffmpeg, never shipped or committed.
renderly-app/dev-assets/

# wasm-pack output (docs/preview-webview.md P3): generated by `npm run build:wasm`,
# served from / in dev and copied into dist/ for release builds. Never committed.
renderly-app/public/wasm-pkg/

# Bundled ffmpeg binaries — fetched per build environment by
# renderly-app/scripts/fetch-ffmpeg.mjs, never committed. Keep the directory's
# README tracked so Tauri's `ffmpeg/*` resource glob always matches.
renderly-app/src-tauri/ffmpeg/**
!renderly-app/src-tauri/ffmpeg/README.md
